      <section anchor="linear-transformation" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-4.2">
        <name slugifiedName="name-linear-transformation">Linear Transformation</name>
        <t indent="0" pn="section-4.2-1">The linear transformation is denoted by l: (V_8)^16 -&gt; V_8, and
defined as:</t>
        <artwork name="" type="" align="left" alt="" pn="section-4.2-2"><![CDATA[
l(a_15,...,a_0) = nabla(148*delta(a_15) + 32*delta(a_15) +
133*delta(a_13) + 16*delta(a_12) + 194*delta(a_11) +
192*delta(a_10) + 1*delta(a_9) + 251*delta(a_8) + 1*delta(a_7) +
192*delta(a_6) + 194*delta(a_5) + 16*delta(a_4) + 133*delta(a_3) +
32*delta(a_2) + 148*delta(a_1) +1*delta(a_0)),
]]></artwork>
        <t indent="0" pn="section-4.2-3">for all a_i belonging to V_8, i = 0, 1, ..., 15, where the addition
and multiplication operations are in the field Q, and constants are
elements of the field as defined above.</t>
      </section>
      <section anchor="transformations" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-4.3">
        <name slugifiedName="name-transformations">Transformations</name>
        <t indent="0" pn="section-4.3-1">The following transformations are applicable for encryption and
decryption algorithms:</t>
        <dl newline="false" spacing="normal" indent="3" pn="section-4.3-2">
          <dt pn="section-4.3-2.1">X[x]:V_128-&gt;V_128</dt>
          <dd pn="section-4.3-2.2">X[k](a)=k(xor)a, where k, a belong to V_128,</dd>
          <dt pn="section-4.3-2.3">S:V_128-&gt; V_128</dt>
          <dd pn="section-4.3-2.4">S(a)=(a_15||...||a_0)=pi(a_15)||...||pi(a_0), where
a_15||...||a_0 belongs to V_128, a_i belongs to V_8, i=0,1,...,15,</dd>
          <dt pn="section-4.3-2.5">S^(-1):V_128-&gt; V_128</dt>
          <dd pn="section-4.3-2.6">the inverse transformation of S, which may be
calculated, for example, as follows:
S^(-1)(a_15||...||a_0)=pi^(-1) (a_15)||...||pi^(-1)(a_0), where
a_15||...||a_0 belongs to V_128, a_i belongs to V_8, i=0,1,...,15,</dd>
          <dt pn="section-4.3-2.7">R:V_128-&gt; V_128</dt>
          <dd pn="section-4.3-2.8">R(a_15||...||a_0)=l(a_15,...,a_0)||a_15||...||a_1,
where a_15||...||a_0 belongs to V_128, a_i belongs to V_8,
i=0,1,...,15,</dd>
          <dt pn="section-4.3-2.9">L:V_128-&gt; V_128</dt>
          <dd pn="section-4.3-2.10">L(a)=R^(16)(a), where a belongs to V_128,</dd>
          <dt pn="section-4.3-2.11">R^(-1):V_128-&gt; V_128</dt>
          <dd pn="section-4.3-2.12">the inverse transformation of R, which may be
calculated, for example, as follows: R^(-1)(a_15||...||a_0)=a_14||
a_13||...||a_0||l(a_14,a_13,...,a_0,a_15), where a_15||...||a_0
belongs to V_128, a_i belongs to V_8, i=0,1,...,15,</dd>
          <dt pn="section-4.3-2.13">L^(-1):V_128-&gt; V_128</dt>
          <dd pn="section-4.3-2.14">L^(-1)(a)=(R^(-1))(16)(a), where a belongs to
V_128, and</dd>
          <dt pn="section-4.3-2.15">F[k]:V_128[*]V_128 -&gt; V_128[*]V_128</dt>
          <dd pn="section-4.3-2.16">F[k](a_1,a_0)=(LSX[k](a_1)(xor)a_0,a_1), where k, a_0, a_1 belong
to V_128.</dd>
        </dl>
      </section>
      <section anchor="key-schedule" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-4.4">
        <name slugifiedName="name-key-schedule">Key Schedule</name>
        <t indent="0" pn="section-4.4-1">Key schedule uses round constants C_i belonging to V_128, i=1, 2,
..., 32, defined as</t>
        <artwork name="" type="" align="left" alt="" pn="section-4.4-2"><![CDATA[
C_i=L(Vec_128(i)), i=1,2,...,32.
]]></artwork>
        <t indent="0" pn="section-4.4-3">Round keys K_i, i=1, 2, ..., 10 are derived from key
K=k_255||...||k_0 belonging to V_256, k_i belongs to V_1, i=0, 1,
..., 255, as follows:</t>
        <artwork name="" type="" align="left" alt="" pn="section-4.4-4"><![CDATA[
K_1=k_255||...||k_128;
K_2=k_127||...||k_0;
(K_(2i+1),K_(2i+2))=F[C_(8(i-1)+8)]...
 F[C_(8(i-1)+1)](K_(2i-1),K_(2i)), i=1,2,3,4.
]]></artwork>
      </section>
      <section anchor="basic-encryption-algorithm" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-4.5">
        <name slugifiedName="name-basic-encryption-algorithm">Basic Encryption Algorithm</name>
        <section anchor="encryption" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-4.5.1">
          <name slugifiedName="name-encryption">Encryption</name>
          <t indent="0" pn="section-4.5.1-1">Depending on the values of round keys K_1,...,K_10, the encryption
algorithm is a substitution E_(K_1,...,K_10) defined as follows:</t>
          <artwork name="" type="" align="left" alt="" pn="section-4.5.1-2"><![CDATA[
E_(K_1,...,K_10)(a)=X[K_10]LSX[K_9]...LSX[K_2]LSX[K_1](a),
]]></artwork>
          <t indent="0" pn="section-4.5.1-3">where a belongs to V_128.</t>
        </section>
        <section anchor="decryption" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-4.5.2">
          <name slugifiedName="name-decryption">Decryption</name>
          <t indent="0" pn="section-4.5.2-1">Depending on the values of round keys K_1,...,K_10, the decryption
algorithm is a substitution D_(K_1,...,K_10) defined as follows:</t>
          <artwork name="" type="" align="left" alt="" pn="section-4.5.2-2"><![CDATA[
D_(K_1,...,K_10)(a)=X[K_1]L^(-1)S^(-1)X[K_2]...
 L^(-1)S^(-1)X[K_9] L^(-1)S^(-1)X[K_10](a),
]]></artwork>
          <t indent="0" pn="section-4.5.2-3">where a belongs to V_128.</t>
        </section>
      </section>
    </section>
